@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title The code-tree migration in progress — the legacy Code/ tree is retired; the FindCare backend is parked, still monolithic, in the interim landing FindCare/Code/; the remaining move is to disperse it into the feature directories that already exist

package "FindCare/Code/ — interim landing (the legacy Code/ tree is gone from disk)" #fdf6f6 {
  component "app.py\nstill one file: 14 @app.post/@app.get routes (~88 KB).\nNot yet dispersed — it already imports\nProviderManagement, SpecialtyFilter,\nClinicalTrials, ProviderDetail, ProviderList." as APP
  component "find_care_facade.py\nprovider_lookup_models.py" as FACADE
  component "embedding_client.py\nduplicates the ChatHealthyLib llm facade\n(BUG-003)" as EMB
  component "prompt_system_maker.py\na prompt-authoring tool" as PSM
  component "safety_service.py\nis_emergency has no call site (BUG-003 / BUG-011)" as SAFETY
  component "tests/test_evalcare_handoff.py" as TESTS
}

package "Destinations already in use" #f5fbfa {
  component "FindCare/<Feature>/\nClinicalTrials, Geo, ParameterDeclaration,\nProviderDetail, ProviderList,\nProviderManagement, SpecialtyFilter" as FINDCARE
  component "sharedServices/Code/<Feature>/\nAboutChatHealthy (+ me/), displayChrome,\nProviderSelection, FacilitySearch, FacilitySelection,\nClinicalTrialSelection, Geo, LockoutTool,\nUtteranceManager, UserParameters, handoffToEvaluateCare" as SHAREDSVC
  component "Website/FindCareChat/\nReact shell (index.html, main.tsx, App.tsx)\n+ the widgets under src/" as WEBSITE
  component "ChatHealthyLib\nchathealthy_lib.llm facade" as LIB
}

component "Destination not stated\nanywhere in the repository" as UNKNOWN #fff8e6

APP --> FINDCARE : the 14 routes join the\nfeature services they\nalready import
FACADE --> FINDCARE : provider-lookup layer
EMB --> LIB : the facade already exists;\nthe duplicate is retired to it
FACADE ..> UNKNOWN : facade vs feature home\nnot settled
EMB ..> UNKNOWN
PSM ..> UNKNOWN
SAFETY ..> UNKNOWN

package "Populations that have already reached a settled home" #f5fbfa {
  component "React shell + widgets\n-> Website/FindCareChat/" as MOVED_SHELL
  component "about-content 'me'\n-> sharedServices/Code/AboutChatHealthy/me" as MOVED_ME
  component "iPhone / UX walkthrough tests\n-> feature tests dirs\n(e.g. FindCare/SpecialtyFilter/tests)" as MOVED_UX
  component "Shared/ops (Caddyfile, certs, ops scripts,\ntools) -> no longer in the authored tree;\nappears only under build staging (/deploy, gitignored)" as MOVED_OPS
}

MOVED_SHELL -[#9ca3af]-> WEBSITE
MOVED_ME -[#9ca3af]-> SHAREDSVC

package "Build tooling — decoupled from the business tree (this leg is done)" #f7f7fb {
  component "architecture/DevOpsBuildDeployAndEnvironmentManagement/\nvite.config.ts, hf_helpers.py,\npreflight_undefined_names.py,\n_deploy_chain.py + build chain" as BUILDTOOL
  component "build_architecture.json\nFindCareChat.source_root = Website/FindCareChat\ndist = build/react/FindCareChat" as BUILDARCH
}

BUILDTOOL --> BUILDARCH : reads source_root here\ninstead of hardcoding Code/ConversationalUX
BUILDTOOL ..> WEBSITE : resolves the React source\nfrom the declared root

note bottom of UNKNOWN
  These files sit in the interim landing without a
  settled feature home. Choosing one is an architecture
  decision, and guessing it here would put an
  unapproved answer into the plan. (Was N48: the shell
  files, iPhone tests and Shared/ops in this note have
  since reached homes; prompt_system_maker.py has not.)
end note

note right of FINDCARE
  Facility work is the exception to the pattern: its
  tools (FacilitySearch, FacilitySelection) sit under
  sharedServices/Code, not under FindCare/, so a
  facility route still has no feature directory in
  FindCare/ to move into. Geo now exists under BOTH
  FindCare/ and sharedServices/Code/ — the dispersal
  must settle that duplication (ties to BUG-003).
end note

note bottom of BUILDTOOL
  The build no longer depends on the business layout.
  vite.config.ts, the build chain and hf_helpers once
  spelled Code/ConversationalUX/FindCareChat/frontend
  in three places; they now read FindCareChat.source_root
  from build_architecture.json. The only ConversationalUX
  string left in _deploy_chain.py is a past-tense comment.
end note

note bottom of APP
  The tree is fully retired only when app.py is broken
  up into the feature directories it imports and nothing
  authored remains under FindCare/Code/. Until then the
  monolith is parked, not migrated.
end note

@enduml
